 "notes": "Combined 95% C.L. upper limit on the ALP-two-photon coupling (NFW profile), the headline result. Extracted as the lower boundary of the blue excluded region (This work curve) in the left panel of Fig.5 (e-print summary_compare.pdf, vector drawing idx 48); identical to the Combined panel of Fig.2. Paper Lagrangian L=-(1/4)g_ag a F Ftilde matches the canonical convention exactly, so no conversion applied. The boundary is intrinsically spiky (fluctuates from ~2e-13 to ~2e-12 due to imperfect sky-line subtraction); reported as median-per-mass-bin over ~97 bins spanning 2.7-5.3 eV. A narrow gap near m~4.15-4.26 eV (blocking filter at 5820-5970 A) is bridged by the plotted line. This is an ALP DM decay search assuming ALPs are all the DM; the bound depends on per-dwarf DM profiles from a Jeans analysis (D-factors), not a single local density, so dm_density_assumed is null. coreNFWtides profile (Fig.4) gives comparable bounds.",
